whisper: Adds up spending from a spreadsheet (CSV) by kind, biggest first.
whisper:   stellanova spending.stella money.csv
whisper: The first row names the columns; it needs columns called date, kind and amount.

use: spreadsheet
use: options.stella

a total has:
  kind (text)
  amount (a number)
and the universe said i love you

to column, given name (text) and heading (a list of text), returning a number:
  set n to position of name in heading
  if n is 0:
    scrawl "The spreadsheet needs a column called '", name, "'."
    end the program with 1
  return n
and the universe said i love you

genesis:
  set files to plain words
  if the size of files is not 1:
    scrawl "Say which spreadsheet, like: stellanova spending.stella money.csv"
    end the program with 1
  set file name to item 1 of files
  if not (file file name exists):
    scrawl "There is no file called ", file name, "."
    end the program with 1
  set rows to rows of the spreadsheet (contents of file file name)
  set heading to item 1 of rows changed by each h becomes lower case of trimmed h
  set kind column to column with ("kind", heading)
  set amount column to column with ("amount", heading)
  set totals to a table of numbers
  set skipped to 0
  for each n from 2 to the size of rows:
    set row to item n of rows
    try:
      set kind to item kind column of row
      set amount to item amount column of row as a number
      if totals contains kind:
        set the entry kind of totals to the entry kind of totals plus amount
      otherwise:
        set the entry kind of totals to amount
    if that went wrong:
      scrawl "Row ", n, " skipped: ", the wound
      set skipped to skipped plus 1
  set sums to a list of totals
  for each kind in keys of totals:
    conjure a total as t
    set the kind of t to kind
    set the amount of t to the entry kind of totals
    add t to sums
  set all to 0
  for each t in sorted sums by amount, biggest first:
    scrawl the kind of t padded to 12 letters, the amount of t rounded to 2 decimal places
    set all to all plus the amount of t
  scrawl "Altogether" padded to 12 letters, all rounded to 2 decimal places
and the universe said i love you
